1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Useful work should leave the browser.
Download the invitation, run of show, checklist or budget as its own PDF.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
A letter you can read.
This is an actual PDF exported by the app from the fictional Cedar demo.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
A filename that makes sense.
Each PDF starts with the event title, then its document name and a unique suffix.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Render keeps the app running.
A Node web service serves the workspace, protects API keys and produces exports.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Two models. Clear roles.
Open-weight Gemma and GPT-OSS interpret notes and propose wording. Humans review the result.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
A public home. Open source.
The .tech address gives judges a direct route to the app. GitHub holds the MIT-licensed source.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Copilot helped review a real fix.
Copilot Chat inspected PDF filenames in PR #1. Its findings were evaluated and regression-tested.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Built to be checked.
145 passing software tests cover app behavior. They do not measure general AI accuracy.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Make room for the event.
Try Flow Point. Read the evidence, edit a sample and open its PDF.
